\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Proposition}
\title{Jacobian compensation in normalized Gaussian transport}
\date{2026-10-29}

\p{Let #{M,M'} be finite-dimensional real positive inner-product
spaces with [induced Euclidean volumes](fdip-002M)
#{\lambda,\lambda'}. Let #{Q,Q'} be positive self-adjoint precisions,
and suppose a linear isomorphism #{T:M\to M'} preserves their actions:
##{\mathcal A_{Q'}(Tx)=\mathcal A_Q(x).}
It need not preserve the reference pairings. Its adjoint uses these
specified inner products, and
##{T^\dagger Q'T=Q,\qquad (Q')^{-1}=TQ^{-1}T^\dagger.}
For its absolute Jacobian #{J(T)>0}, one has
##{\begin{aligned}
T_*\lambda&=J(T)^{-1}\lambda',\\
Z_{Q'}&=J(T)Z_Q,\qquad T_*\mu_Q=\mu_{Q'}.
\end{aligned}}
For every real or complex Borel observable #{F'},
##{\int|F'|\,d\mu_{Q'}=\int|F'\circ T|\,d\mu_Q}
as extended nonnegative integrals. Hence integrability is equivalent
on the two sides, and, under that condition,
#{\omega_{Q'}(F')=\omega_Q(F'\circ T)}.}

\proof{
\p{Polarization of the preserved real quadratic forms gives
#{T^\dagger Q'T=Q}; taking inverses gives the stated inverse-precision
identity. Choose orthonormal charts #{C:M\to\mathbb R^n} and
#{C':M'\to\mathbb R^n}. By the [induced-volume convention](fdip-002M),
both charts carry volume to coordinate Lebesgue measure. Identify
the chart targets with counting spaces and apply the
[reference-volume change formula](fdip-002K) to #{C'TC^{-1}}.
Its Gram determinant equals that of #{T^\dagger T}, so the absolute
Jacobian is #{J(T)=\sqrt{\det(T^\dagger T)}}. Transporting the
formula back through the charts gives the pushforward of volume,
equivalently
#{\int h'\,d\lambda'=J(T)\int h'\circ T\,d\lambda}
for every nonnegative Borel #{h'}. Apply it to the Gaussian weight;
action preservation gives #{Z_{Q'}=J(T)Z_Q}. Both normalizers are
finite and positive by \ref{fdip-002T}. For a nonnegative Borel
#{h'}, divide the same substitution by this equality:
##{\begin{aligned}
\int h'\,d\mu_{Q'}
 &=\frac{J(T)}{Z_{Q'}}\int h'(Tx)e^{-\mathcal A_Q(x)}\,d\lambda(x)\\
 &=\int h'\circ T\,d\mu_Q.
\end{aligned}}
Indicators of Borel sets prove the event-pushforward statement.
Taking #{h'=|F'|} proves the extended absolute-integral equality.
Only when finite do positive/negative parts, and for complex functions
real/imaginary parts, give the stated expectation identity.}
}

\p{The inverse-precision identity is covariance congruence for the
specified pairings, not generally operator similarity. The
[orthonormal-basis realization](fdip-00KH) gives its transpose formula
and the covariance-parameter provider correspondence. The
[quadratic-isometry example](fdip-000Z) shows that this normalized
transport can lose both counting-pairing and retained-projection
compatibility. Such maps are not enriched background arrows.}

\p{The volume convention is
\citet{Exercises 1.2.20-22, p. 41}{tao2011measure}; the covariance-parameter
Gaussian substitution is
\citet{Proposition B.55, p. 505}{friedli2017statistical}.
The [inverse-precision covariance theorem](fdip-000B) identifies its
covariance with #{Q^{-1}} for these reference pairings.}
